  "sourceFacts": {
    "horizontalBasis": "Shared campus Q192988 plus declared way268533454/native35184640622286, named Telescope Gallery. Contiguous way268533446/native35184640622278 is named The Transit House; ways268533457/459 continue east toward the separate Great Equatorial building. Integral parts1459032942/943/944 supply western8m/5m/5m bands. Own anchor raw[-17,1], internalX east,Z south, heading0 baked into native coordinates. Only these seven records are owned; retain separate dome way268533517 and southwest annex way268533460.",
    "architecturalHeights": "Mapped8m central west part/eastern ranges and5m low parts/link are unqualified overall controls. Working low eaves3.65m/ridges5m, central transit eaves5.6m/ridges8m, east eaves6.2m/ridge8m and small photo-led silver cap to9.1m. The small silver cap is reconstructed behind the eastern transit/galleries junction after comparing the north and south pictures. Its precise position is not mapped. Other roof/shutter/window/arch inventories and hidden elevations are reconstructed. Brown-tinted shared slate substitutes for weathered tiles. No furnished instruments/interiors, active shutters, copied lettering/banners or certified Prime Meridian survey alignment."
